course: dictionary
lesson: 10692
title: Unripe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «The bananas on the tree are still unripe, so they are green and hard.» Unripe means not ready to eat yet. The word starts with un-, which often means not, and ripe means ready to eat.
explain: Use the clues around the word. Green and hard are signs that the fruit is not ready. Unripe fruit is often hard and sour, and in «Unripe fruits are often green, hard and sour so animals do not eat them before the seeds are ready», the sour taste keeps animals away.
explain: Ripe fruit is the opposite of unripe. Ripe fruit turns soft, sweet and bright. Fruit can change over time, so an unripe fruit may become ripe later.
fact: Unripe means not ready to eat yet.
fact: «Unripe fruit is more acidic; as fruit ripens, sugar goes up and acid goes down.»
fact: Some fruit keeps ripening even after it has been picked.
fact: Unripe fruit can give you a tummy ache, so wait until it is ripe before you eat it.
exercise: «Unripe fruit is more acidic; as fruit ripens, sugar goes up and acid goes down.» What happens to the sugar as fruit ripens? | *Sugar goes up | Sugar goes down | Sugar stays exactly the same | Sugar disappears
exercise: Maths: a basket has 12 plums and 5 of them are unripe. How many plums are ripe? | 12 | *7 | 5 | 17
exercise: «Unripe fruits are often green, hard and sour so animals do not eat them before the seeds are ready.» Why do animals leave unripe fruit alone? | *Because it is hard and sour, and the seeds are not ready yet | Because it is soft and sweet | Because it is bright red and juicy
test: Science: some fruit still ripens after it is picked. What does this tell you? | Fruit only ripens on the tree | Fruit stops changing the moment it is picked | *Fruit can keep ripening after it is picked | Fruit turns to stone when it is picked
test: Health: why should you be careful about eating too much unripe fruit? | It turns your skin green | It makes you grow taller overnight | *It can give you a tummy ache | It makes the fruit ripe in your stomach
exam: Mia says «unripe» means rotten. What does it really mean? | *Not ready to eat yet | Rotten and brown | Sold in a shop | Very sweet and juicy
